{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01018",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.68,
      "end_seconds": 5.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Right, uh, hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.54,
      "end_seconds": 14.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 16.69,
      "end_seconds": 22.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Ah, doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.67,
      "end_seconds": 29.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Mainly I've been repeating the same questions. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.36,
      "end_seconds": 37.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Alright, when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.72,
      "end_seconds": 40.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "I'd say two weeks, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 44.79,
      "end_seconds": 51.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "I, I think it's been nearer three weeks, um, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.59,
      "end_seconds": 57.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly two to three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.05,
      "end_seconds": 65.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "Yeah, roughly. Erm, uh, I'd been misplacing things, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.21,
      "end_seconds": 71.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Right, did you get weakness on one side or hallucinations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.96,
      "end_seconds": 78.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Um, no, no weakness on one side or hallucinations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.14,
      "end_seconds": 85.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Have you had any falls, trouble with bladder control or low mood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.95,
      "end_seconds": 89.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Mm, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.99,
      "end_seconds": 92.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.29,
      "end_seconds": 95.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.09,
      "end_seconds": 100.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "So, anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.79,
      "end_seconds": 105.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.68,
      "end_seconds": 127.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 129.9,
      "end_seconds": 145.21,
      "duration_seconds": 15.31,
      "text": "It's glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar, doctor. Ah, um, he is on metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.12,
      "end_seconds": 150.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.08,
      "end_seconds": 156.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "I've had diabetes, yes. I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.57,
      "end_seconds": 166.27,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Right, so diabetes and high blood pressure are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.16,
      "end_seconds": 170.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "No, uh, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.06,
      "end_seconds": 172.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.31,
      "end_seconds": 175.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.79,
      "end_seconds": 179.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.58,
      "end_seconds": 184.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.06,
      "end_seconds": 191.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Okay, how are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.24,
      "end_seconds": 197.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.36,
      "end_seconds": 202.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.82,
      "end_seconds": 209.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.2,
      "end_seconds": 213.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.51,
      "end_seconds": 218.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.76,
      "end_seconds": 225.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.1,
      "end_seconds": 242.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.83,
      "end_seconds": 262.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 98 percent on room air, pulse 85, blood pressure 121 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.23,
      "end_seconds": 267.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.18,
      "end_seconds": 271.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.51,
      "end_seconds": 288.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Your gait is steady and the tone in your limbs is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.5,
      "end_seconds": 295.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.83,
      "end_seconds": 323.04,
      "duration_seconds": 13.21,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, this is probably memory difficulties that need to be worked up. It could also be early dementia, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.32,
      "end_seconds": 326.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.85,
      "end_seconds": 338.43,
      "duration_seconds": 10.58,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with memory difficulties that need to be worked up do well once it's treated properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.86,
      "end_seconds": 351.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "I'll request a thyroid test, it'll help with memory loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.09,
      "end_seconds": 353.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Mm, alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.02,
      "end_seconds": 366.91,
      "duration_seconds": 11.89,
      "text": "Keep a daily routine and write things down, a notebook by the door works well. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.37,
      "end_seconds": 372.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Hm, okay. I'm going to send a referral to the memory clinic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.49,
      "end_seconds": 378.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Could I get blood tests done? A friend had it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.92,
      "end_seconds": 396.41,
      "duration_seconds": 16.49,
      "text": "Not at this point, no. It isn't indicated yet. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently. I'd like to see you again after the results are back. So, have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.05,
      "end_seconds": 402.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Erm, great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.16,
      "end_seconds": 405.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}